# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for cppverify-sanitize.sh in thread mode: data
# races inside Z3 4.13.4 itself, and LLVM's crash handler. Each names a
# function of Z3 or LLVM that the verifier does not call itself.
#
# Every Z3 command context, which pattern inference makes for each quantified
# query, sets the global verbose stream (util.cpp) without a lock.
race:set_verbose_stream
# Z3's statistics read its global allocation counters without the lock its
# allocator updates them under (memory_manager.cpp).
race:get_memory_statistics
# A check's timeout handler sets its flag from Z3's timer thread without
# synchronization, and Z3_interrupt, which may be called from any thread,
# reads it (cancel_eh.h).
race:cancel_eh
# A nested Z3 timer locks the timer pool's mutex while the outer timer holds
# its state's mutex, and the pool hands a free state to a new timer by
# locking the state's mutex under its own. A state is free only once its
# timer has released it, so the two orders never meet; TSan relates the
# recycled states (scoped_timer.cpp).
deadlock:scoped_timer
# LLVM prints a backtrace after a fatal signal, which is not
# async-signal-safe; only crash_report_url.cpp crashes on purpose.
signal:PrintStackTraceSignalHandler
